\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Network-specific direction--coverage diagnostic for wiki-Vote at $W=1280$. (A) Standard PageRank scores incoming-link importance, whereas the simulation propagates along stored voter-to-votee arcs; the node motifs are explanatory rather than a sampled subgraph. (B) The default PageRank-4k pool covers none of the five full-reference seeds on each of the five paths. (C) Independent 10,000-world evaluation gives mean incremental spreads of 55.73602 nodes for the full reference and 15.04268 for PageRank-4k, a paired difference of $-40.69334$ nodes (73.01\% loss). These coverage and degree facts are consistent with an incoming-ranking/outgoing-propagation mismatch under the recorded orientation. No reverse-orientation intervention was performed, so the figure does not identify a unique causal mechanism or make a general claim about PageRank.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:direction-mechanism}{{1}{3}{Network-specific direction--coverage diagnostic for wiki-Vote at $W=1280$. (A) Standard PageRank scores incoming-link importance, whereas the simulation propagates along stored voter-to-votee arcs; the node motifs are explanatory rather than a sampled subgraph. (B) The default PageRank-4k pool covers none of the five full-reference seeds on each of the five paths. (C) Independent 10,000-world evaluation gives mean incremental spreads of 55.73602 nodes for the full reference and 15.04268 for PageRank-4k, a paired difference of $-40.69334$ nodes (73.01\% loss). These coverage and degree facts are consistent with an incoming-ranking/outgoing-propagation mismatch under the recorded orientation. No reverse-orientation intervention was performed, so the figure does not identify a unique causal mechanism or make a general claim about PageRank}{figure.1}{}}
